xdg-desktop-portal-gnome — FeralOS shadow dummy
===============================================

This package is deliberately EMPTY. It shadows Alpine's real
xdg-desktop-portal-gnome (a GNOME / mutter-dependent portal backend that
also drags in nautilus) so that it is never installed on FeralOS.

Why:
- Alpine's niri-portalsconf subpackage (part of the niri package) declares
  depend = xdg-desktop-portal-gnome in niri-portals.conf's APK metadata.
  This version-999 dummy satisfies that dependency without pulling the
  real backend (999 beats any Alpine version).
- FeralOS serves every portal interface its desktops use through
  xdg-desktop-portal-gtk (FileChooser, Settings, Notification, Print,
  Access, Account, Inhibit, Lockdown, Email, AppChooser, DynamicLauncher,
  Wallpaper) and xdg-desktop-portal-wlr (Screenshot, ScreenCast).
- Only RemoteDesktop and GlobalShortcuts are lost — both unused on FeralOS.
- The Secret portal is served by gnome-keyring / oo7 through their own
  .portal files, not through the gnome portal backend.
